                    {
                        "translation_id": "992bd3f2-da33-44ee-aa12-af7cb72c2caa",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7e8a02c-77a9-3913-934a-41eb6f1865da",
                        "source_sense_id": "442c970c-5d3d-3486-97c3-105a58d139ae",
                        "target_lang_word": "phanerogam",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "phanerogam",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "019eef83-1ff1-3c4f-a49a-d81491ca97c6",
                                        "entry_id": "74321daa-8636-3cb1-8c5a-6e30ddd800b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any plant that produces seeds (rather than spores)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c39f974-7699-4ec3-8eb3-204d1d4b7829",
                                                "sense_id": "019eef83-1ff1-3c4f-a49a-d81491ca97c6",
                                                "text": "Among phanerogams (seed plants), only two orders of gymnosperms, the Cycadales and the Ginkgoales, have ciliated motile sperm cells; all others (higher gymnosperms and angiosperms) have nonmotile sperm cells or sperm nuclei."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9524c2e-8a32-4555-807f-bcf999444ac2",
                                                "sense_id": "019eef83-1ff1-3c4f-a49a-d81491ca97c6",
                                                "text": "The stomach contents of the Selerikanka horse contained 116 taxa: 96 phanerogams, 20 cryptogams. Among the phanerogams were 12 tree species, 14 species of shrubs and dwarf-shrubs, as well as 72 species of herbs and very small dwarf-shrubs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c26b904-3ed5-4977-a0d3-e7f7ee7f4b84",
                                                "sense_id": "019eef83-1ff1-3c4f-a49a-d81491ca97c6",
                                                "text": "Generally speaking, the ranges of most cryptogams are geographically broader than those of phanerogams, and many more species are widely disjunct over the world."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80ee2ee8-2991-4438-a4d3-862120421ca6",
                        "source_entry_id": "e7e8a02c-77a9-3913-934a-41eb6f1865da",
